**Pipeline expectations.** Separation of variables (C7, PDE stretch goal) gives $u = 100\,e^{-\alpha\pi^2 t/L^2}\sin(\pi x/L)$. If PDE solving is not built, the result must fall back to a numeric method-of-lines solve and say so. The midpoint falls to $50$ K above ambient at $t \approx 702.3\ \mathrm s$. The check $u_t - \alpha u_{xx} = 0$ is confirmed symbolically. The 3D surface $u(x, t)$ renders.
